  "evidence": {
    "coin_block_fields": "Block_Animate uses the unsigned halfword at +0x12 as a per-frame timer and byte +0x18 as a four-frame index. DrawBlocks tests +0x16; Phase_State2/3 test +0x17 before dispatching the block state. Widths and offsets retained.",
    "coin_countdown": "The old base &mSparkles[31].y is scene +0x5000; indices 0x73 and 0x72 address +0x51cc and +0x51c8, the existing mCountdown and mPhase. Native member operations emit the same output.",
    "coin_priority": "RenderOamBothScreens forwards its fifth parameter to OAM priority, as defined in d_s_mg_base.cpp.",
    "roulette_models": "include/dScMgRoulette_c.h explicitly destroys the 0x50-byte records at +0x531c/+0x536c with ModelD1. Their offsets relative to the slider at +0x530c are +0x10/+0x60. Model.h identifies slot3 as UpdateVerts and slot5 as Render(const Vector3*).",
    "snowball_coordinates": "Both collision tests select a tile by x lane * 0x5c0 plus course row * 2; within-tile coordinates feed diagonal sum/difference comparisons. UpdateSnowball copies one sample separately for wall, breakable and water tests before collecting collision-response vectors.",
